      "content": "Peroxide is a great idea, but I'd recommend taking it a step further. You're going to want to apply some antibiotic ointment to the wound, and then cover it with a bandage. I'm not saying you need to go to the doctor, but I do recommend a quick visit to get a tetanus shot, just to be safe. And while you're at it, you might as well take a few aspirin to reduce the swelling.",
